Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 00:16:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 66/67] Move Qt to obs-deps 2026-10-23 for the macOS 27.2
 startup crash

On the macOS 27.2 beta LiveHime 0.3.1 crashed on every launch: resetting
the cursor goes through QImage::toCGImage(), which in Qt 6.11.1 hands
CGImageCreate a color space that was already released (QTBUG-147602), and
CoreGraphics traps on it. obs-deps 2026-10-23 ships the same Qt 6.11.1 with
Qt's fix for it; take its Qt build (only the Qt6 dependency changes).

patch-qcocoa.sh now applies obs-deps' own Qt patches for macOS (copied
from that release, checksums as in its qt6.zsh) before the tray icon fix,
so the rebuilt Cocoa plugin comes from the same sources as the rest of Qt.

Reported by AzzzRChie with a diagnosis and a working workaround.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
